## Config
- Frontend apps (`apps/web`) use **Playwright E2E only** — no Vitest/Testing Library unit or integration tests
- No webServer; URLs from `PLAYWRIGHT_APP_URL` / `PLAYWRIGHT_API_URL` (env or `--app` / `--api` params)
- Fastify: only `--api` param; `test:e2e` = URL-based, `test:e2e:local` = spawn API, poll, run, cleanup
- Param format: `--app=URL` or `--app URL`, `--api=URL` or `--api URL`
- CI: test:e2e:local only (spawn local servers; no Vercel URLs)
- Local: Next `test:e2e:local` = spawn Fastify + Next, poll, run, kill. Fastify `test:e2e:local` = spawn API only. Root `pnpm test:e2e` = run both via scripts/run-e2e.mjs
- workers: 1, fullyParallel: false — PGLite does not support concurrent writers; tests must run in series
- projects: setup first (auth), then chromium (tests using storageState)

## Dynamic Sandbox (Web, Mathler)
- Auth via `auth.setup.ts`: runs before chromium project, saves `storageState` to `playwright/.auth/user.json`
- Use `loginWithDynamicSandbox` from `@repo/e2e-helpers` — navigates, fills email/OTP, waits for `authSuccessSelector`
- Env: `E2E_TEST_EMAIL`, `E2E_STATIC_OTP` (from [Dynamic Test Accounts](https://docs.dynamic.xyz/developer-dashboard/test-accounts))
- Web: `authSuccessSelector: 'text=Signed In'`, `loginPath: '/auth/login'`
- Mathler: `authSuccessSelector: 'h1:has-text("Mathler")'`, `loginPath: '/'`
- Root `pnpm test:e2e` runs API E2E, Web E2E, Mathler E2E via scripts/run-e2e.mjs

## Session Model
- Context = browser profile; authenticatedPage = single shared page reused across all authed tests (worker-scoped)
- One login per worker, then navigate and assert. No per-test login for authed tests
- Session reused via worker-scoped storageState (saved after login, new context per test)
## Test Order
- Setup project first: `auth.setup.ts` (Dynamic sandbox or magic-link). Use `/auth/login` for login page when applicable
- Chromium project: chat-assistant, wallets, app (use authenticatedPage; storageState from setup)
- Security project: authenticator, passkeys, api-keys (use authenticatedPage; TOTP spec uses extractSessionToken for test endpoint)

## Auth Fixtures
- Login/logout tests: import `@playwright/test`, use `page` (fresh context per test)
- Authed feature tests: import from `e2e/fixtures`, use `authenticatedPage`; no `loginAsTestUser` in test body
- Each authed test must navigate to its target route (e.g. `authenticatedPage.goto('/')`) since the same page is reused

## Test Email
- Use `test@test.ai` when `ALLOW_TEST` enabled; token from DB (`/test/magic-link/last`), no fake outbox. Only E2E magic-link flow requires `@test.ai`.
